  "title": "Usage and register label normalisation map for the CDSL dictionaries",
  "note": "Maps every CDSL markup label that states a word's USAGE or REGISTER (as opposed to its grammar, its citation source, or a purely editorial aside) onto one closed vocabulary. Consumed by scripts/build-usage-register-census.mjs. A label is matched on the exact (tag, token) pair because the same token means different things in different tags and dictionaries: <ab>lit. is always English 'literally', while <lang>Lit. is Lithuanian; <ab>ep. is 'epithet', while <lang>ep. is 'epic'; <lang>L. in AP is Latin, while <ls>L. in MW is the lexicographers hedge.",
